{"name":"Eden","hex":"#266255","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Eden","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A garden built by God as the home for Adam and Eve; sometimes identified as part of Mesopotamia.","An English surname, probably derived from a place name."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A paradise on Earth.","A state of innocence."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Eden"}],"entries":[{"title":"Garden of Eden","blocks":[{"text":"The Garden of Eden, also called Garden of God or the (Terrestrial) Paradise, is the biblical paradise described in Genesis 2–3 and Ezekiel 28 and 31."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Jan_Brueghel_de_Oude_en_Peter_Paul_Rubens_-_Het_aards_paradijs_met_de_zondeval_van_Adam_en_Eva.jpg/330px-Jan_Brueghel_de_Oude_en_Peter_Paul_Rubens_-_Het_aards_paradijs_met_de_zondeval_van_Adam_en_Eva.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden_of_Eden"},{"title":"Eden, New South Wales","blocks":[{"text":"Eden is a coastal town in the South Coast region of New South Wales, Australia. The town is 478 kilometres (297 mi) south of the state capital Sydney and is the most southerly town in New South Wales, located between Nullica Bay to the south and Calle Calle Bay, the northern reach of Twofold Bay, and built on undulating land adjacent to the third-deepest natural harbour in the southern hemisphere, and Snug Cove on its western boundary. At the 2021 census, Eden had a population of 3,425."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/CountryTown0018.jpg/330px-CountryTown0018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eden%2C_New_South_Wales"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/James_Jacques_Joseph_Tissot_-_Adam_and_Eve_Driven_From_Paradise_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/